.TH WC 1.SH NAMEwc \- count lines, words and characters.SH SYNOPSIS\fBwc\fR[\-l] [\-w] [\-c] [file ...].SH DESCRIPTION\fBwc\fRprints the number of lines, words and characters in each file named,and a total when there is more than one:.nf      3      3     14 f1      3      3     14 f2      6      6     28 total.fiA line is counted at a carriage return or a line feed, so OS-9 text andUnix text both count right.  With no file it reads the standard input..SH OPTIONS.TP 12\fB\-l\fRlines only..TP 12\fB\-w\fRwords only..TP 12\fB\-c\fRcharacters only..SH SEE ALSOcharcnt, sum